---
<Base title="Now" description="What Nihal Sulaiman is working on right now: job search, current projects, Kaggle competitions and what he's learning.">
  <PageHero title="What I'm doing now" crumbs={[{ label: 'Now' }]} lead="A snapshot of my current work, updated whenever something changes. Inspired by the nownownow.com idea.">
    <p class="updated" style="margin-top:12px">Last updated 5 November 2026 · Niagara Falls, Ontario</p>
  </PageHero>
  <main>
    <div class="now-grid">
      <div class="card"><h2><i></i>Activity log</h2><p>Every piece of work, numbered and colour-coded by project, is on its own page.</p><p><a href="/log/">Open the activity log →</a></p></div>
      <div class="card"><h2><i></i>Looking for work</h2><p>Data analyst, BI developer, data scientist or ML roles anywhere in Ontario: full-time, part-time or internship, on site or remote. Any sector: retail, finance, logistics, healthcare, hospitality and more.</p><p><a href="/nihal-sulaiman-cv.pdf" type="application/pdf">CV (PDF) →</a> · <a href="/about/cv/">on this site</a></p></div>
      <div class="card"><h2><i></i>Working</h2><p>Remote Data Engineer with Shipd by DataCurve, building training data and coding challenges for AI models.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h2><i></i>Building</h2><ul class="tight"><li><a href="/projects/self-healing-pipelines/">Self-healing pipelines</a>: next is a reference pipeline in Dagster with a fault injector, so the agents can be scored on real failures instead of a simulation.</li><li>Turning the <a href="/projects/bi-toolkit/">BI toolkit</a> into scheduled ETL pipelines that load an Azure SQL Database.</li><li>Tools for each of my <a href="/fields/">eight fields</a>, starting with retail, logistics and health.</li><li>More seeds and fields for <a href="/swarm/">Swarm Intelligence</a>, my flagship.</li><li>This site and blog.</li></ul></div>
      <div class="card"><h2><i></i>Learning</h2><ul class="tight"><li>Working through my own courses: <a href="/learn/etl-course/">Pipeline to Dashboard</a> and <a href="/learn/big-data-cloud/">Data at Scale</a> (Spark, Google Cloud, Kafka).</li><li>T-SQL and SQL Server, my main gap to close.</li><li>Power BI and DAX.</li><li>dbt and dimensional modelling, Dagster for orchestration.</li></ul></div>
      <div class="card"><h2><i></i>Competing</h2><ul class="tight"><li><a href="/projects/name-that-llm/">Name That LLM</a>, ends January 2027</li><li><a href="/projects/casmi-2026/">Enveda CASMI 2026</a>, ends December 2026</li><li><a href="/projects/smart-buildings/">NeurIPS Smart Buildings</a>, ends January 2027</li><li><a href="/projects/squares-in-squares/">Squares in Squares</a>, ends July 2027</li></ul></div>
      <div class="card"><h2><i></i>Writing</h2><p>Latest: <a href="/blog/self-healing-pipelines/">pipelines that fix themselves</a> and a <a href="/blog/doomsday-2026-restudy/">restudy of the 1960 Doomsday paper</a>. Next: write-ups of each Kaggle competition as it ends. <a href="/blog/">Read the blog →</a></p></div>
    </div>
